Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:15:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Local: drag the window from empty sidebar space

On desktop, the empty space below the thread list now moves the window, like
the title bar. The thread list no longer stretches to fill the sidebar;
an invisible filler takes the leftover height and carries the existing
drag-region class. It shrinks to nothing once the list scrolls, so rows,
hover, context menus and drag-and-drop reordering are untouched. Web and
mobile are unchanged.
---
 apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
index 1ed3065a92c..1836ff104d3 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
@@ -3201,7 +3201,7 @@ export default function Sidebar({ routeReveal }: { routeReveal: SidebarRouteReve
           </SidebarGroup>
         }
       >
-        <SidebarGroup className="flex-1" role="presentation">
+        <SidebarGroup role="presentation">
           {isSearchingThreads ? (
             threadSearchResults.length > 0 ? (
               <TooltipProvider
@@ -3640,6 +3640,7 @@ export default function Sidebar({ routeReveal }: { routeReveal: SidebarRouteReve
             </div>
           ) : null}
         </SidebarGroup>
+        {isElectron ? <div aria-hidden className="drag-region min-h-0 flex-1" /> : null}
       </SidebarContent>
       <SidebarChromeFooter />
     </>
